The ordering constraints force two chains: Ivo before Ann before Elif before Gus before Hana, and Finn before Ben before Dev with Cara immediately after Dev. Cara and Elif differ by exactly two slots. Dev is at least slot 4, and Elif needs two later slots for Gus and Hana, so the only placement that leaves room for both chains is Elif 5, Dev 6, Cara 7, Gus 8, Hana 9. Slots 1–4 are then Ivo, Finn, Ann, and Ben. Separation forces Finn in 2 and {Ivo, Ben} = {1, 4}; Finn before Ben puts Ivo in 1, Ann in 3, and Ben in 4. Every other Dev–Cara block breaks an ordering or separation constraint. Hana in 8 and Gus in 9 breaks Gus before Hana.

